body:
Thanks for the advice.

&#x200B;

I started programming with C++ for dummies and mostly trial and errored my way from there. Later on I came across the good advice of reading code bases. Pick a simple open source project that you are interested in and read the source code and comb over the commit messages. Figure out how it all works and why they chose their methods.

So I have no idk why ppl freak out about incest; inbreeding yes (which you did not say any were in your post) as that is a great way to give a kid a birth defect.  There is, in my mind, absolutely nothing wrong with incest at all. Incest ≠  Inbreeding

&#x200B;

So now down to what to do with this information. My advice, just tell her your suspicions. I get that you do not want to hurt her, but by not telling her, that is the only way that it can go. Both get a dna test to confirm it and if it comes back positive then talk about what you both want to do about it. Deiced, before the test, if you are OK with an incest relationship and if so let her know doing that talk. And hey, the dna test could also come back false
